# Architecture

Keep the engine reusable across target languages. Do not hardcode language-specific behavior into shared screens or widgets.

## Layout

- `lib/app/`: application shell only
- `lib/core/`: shared constants, theme, and utilities with no feature logic
- `lib/data/`: local models, local sources, repository implementations
- `lib/domain/`: entities and repository contracts
- `lib/features/`: feature modules; each feature owns its UI, state, and feature-specific logic

## Offline-first

All core learning flows must work with bundled or locally stored data. Do not require network for core functionality.

## Data-driven content

Learning content (lessons, items, copy variants, language packs) must come from data, not from widgets.

```dart
// BAD
Text(targetLanguage == 'es' ? 'Hola' : 'Hello');

// GOOD
Text(item.prompt);
```

## No duplicated business logic

Put rules in domain/data layers or a single shared function. Widgets may format and display results, not reimplement scoring, progress, or content selection.

Language-specific extras (scripts, input methods, phonetics) stay behind feature or content-module boundaries.
